    {'heading': '11.9 · Viśvānara and Indra'},
    {'padas': ["pra vo mahe mandamānāyāndhaso'rcā viśvānarāya viśvābhuve |", 'indrasya yasya sumakhaṃ saho mahi śravo nṛmṇaṃ ca rodasī saparyataḥ ||', "prārcata [ yūyaṃ ] stutiṃ mahate'ndhaso'nnasya dātre | mandamānāya modamānāya stūyamānāya śabdāyamānāyeti vā | viśvānarāya sarvaṃ vibhūtāya | indrasya yasya prītau sumahadbalam | mahacca śravaṇīyaṃ yaśaḥ | nṛmṇaṃ ca balaṃ nṛnatam | dyāvāpṛthivyau vaḥ paricarata iti |", 'kamanyaṃ madhyamādevamavakṣyat |', 'tasyaiṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 9 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.50.1: sing to the great, joyful Viśvānara, giver of food, whose might heaven and earth serve. Who but the god of the mid-air?', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.10 · Viśvānara Savitṛ; Dhātṛ'},
    {'padas': ['udu jyotiramṛtaṃ viśvajanyaṃ viśvānaraḥ savitā devo aśret ||', 'udaśiśriyat | jyotiḥ | amṛtam | sarvajanyam | viśvānaraḥ savitā deva iti |', 'dhātā sarvasya vidhātā | tasyaiṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 10 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 7.76.1: Viśvānara, god Savitṛ, raised the immortal light for all men. Dhātṛ, the disposer of all.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.11 · Dhātṛ; Vidhātṛ'},
    {'padas': ['dhātā dadātu dāśuṣe prācīṃ jīvātumakṣitām |', 'vayaṃ devasya dhīmahi sumatiṃ satyadharmaṇaḥ ||', 'dhātā dadātu dattavate pravṛddhāṃ jīvikāmanupakṣīṇām | vayaṃ devasya dhīmahi sumatiṃ kalyāṇīṃ matiṃ satyadharmaṇaḥ |', 'vidhātā dhātrā vyākhyātaḥ | tasyaiṣa nipāto bhavati bahudevatāyāmṛci'], 'num': '|| 11 ||', 'gloss': 'Atharvaveda-like verse: may Dhātṛ give the giver unfailing life; may we gain the favour of the god of true law. Vidhātṛ, explained with Dhātṛ, appears in passing in a verse to many gods.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.12 · The many-god verse'},
    {'padas': ['somasya rājño varuṇasya dharmaṇi bṛhaspateranumatyā u śarmaṇi |', 'tavāhamadya maghavannupastutau dhātarvidhātaḥ kalaśāṁ abhakṣayam ||', 'ityetābhirdevatābhirabhiprasūtaḥ somakalaśānabhakṣayamiti | kalaśaḥ [ kasmāt ] | kalā asmiñcherate mātrāḥ | kaliśca kalāśca kirateḥ | vikīrṇamātrāḥ'], 'num': '|| 12 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.167.3: by the law of King Soma and Varuṇa, in the shelter of Bṛhaspati and Anumati, praised by you, Maghavan, Dhātṛ and Vidhātṛ, I have drunk the soma-jars. Kalaśa.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.13 · The groups of the mid-air; the Maruts'},
    {'padas': ['athāto madhyasthānā devagaṇāḥ | teṣāṃ marutaḥ prathamāgāmino bhavanti | maruto mitarāviṇo vā | mitarocino vā | mahad dravantīti vā | teṣāmeṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 13 ||', 'gloss': 'Now the groups of gods of the mid-air, first the Maruts: "of measured sound", "of measured light", or "running greatly". Ṛgveda 1.88.1: come, Maruts, with your lightning chariots, horse-winged, like birds with abundant food.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.14 · The Rudras'},
    {'padas': ['ā vidyunmadbhirmarutaḥ svarkai rathebhiryāta ṛṣṭimadbhiraśvaparṇaiḥ |', 'ā varṣiṣṭhayā na iṣā vayo na paptatā sumāyāḥ ||', "vidyunmadbhirmarutaḥ | svarkaiḥ svañcanairiti vā | svarcanairiti vā | svarcibhiriti vā | rathairāyāta | ṛṣṭimadbhiḥ | aśvaparṇairaśvapatanaiḥ | varṣiṣṭhena ca no'nnena vaya ivāpatata | sumāyāḥ kalyāṇakarmāṇo vā | kalyāṇaprajñā vā |", 'rudrā vyākhyātāḥ | teṣāmeṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 14 ||', 'gloss': 'The Rudras, already explained.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.15 · The Rudras; the Ṛbhus'},
    {'padas': ['ā rudrāsa indravantaḥ sajoṣaso hiraṇyarathāḥ suvitāya gantana |', 'iyaṃ vo asmatprati haryate matistṛṣṇaje na diva utsā udanyave ||', "āgacchata rudrā indreṇa | sahajoṣaṇāḥ | suvitāya karmaṇe | iyaṃ vo'smadapi pratikāmayate matiḥ | tṛṣṇaja iva diva utsā udanyave | tṛṣṇak tṛṣyateḥ | udanyurudanyateḥ |", 'ṛbhava uru bhāntīti vā | ṛtena bhāntīti vā | ṛtena bhavantīti vā | teṣāmeṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 15 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 5.57.1: come, Rudras, with Indra, on golden chariots, as springs of heaven to the thirsty. The Ṛbhus: "shining widely", "shining by order", "being by order".', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.16 · The Ṛbhus who won immortality'},
    {'padas': ['viṣṭvī śamī taraṇitvena vāghato martāsaḥ santo amṛtatvamānaśuḥ |', 'saudhanvanā ṛbhavaḥ sūracakṣasaḥ saṃvatsare samapṛcyanta dhītibhiḥ ||', "kṛtvā karmāṇi kṣipratvena | voḷhāro medhāvino vā | martāsaḥ santo'mṛtatvamānaśire | saudhanvanā ṛbhavaḥ sūrakhyānā vā | sūraprajñā vā | saṃvatsare samapṛcyanta [ dhītibhiḥ ] karmabhiḥ |", 'ṛbhurvibhvā vāja iti sudhanvana āṅgirasasya trayaḥ putrā babhūvuḥ | teṣāṃ prathamottamābhyāṃ bahuvannigamā bhavanti na madhyamena | tadetadṛbhośca bahuvacanena camasasya ca saṃstavena bahūni daśatayīṣu sūktāni bhavanti |', "ādityaraśmayo'pyṛbhava ucyante |", 'agohyasya yadasastanā gṛhe tadadyedamṛbhavo nānu gacchatha |', "agohya ādityo'gūhanīyaḥ | tasya yadasvapatha gṛhe | yāvattatra bhavatha na tāvadiha bhavatheti |", 'aṅgiraso vyākhyātāḥ | teṣāmeṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 16 ||', 'gloss': "Ṛgveda 1.110.4: by their quick works the mortal Ṛbhus, sons of Sudhanvan, won immortality and in a year joined the gods. Ṛbhu, Vibhvan and Vāja were the three sons of Sudhanvan Āṅgirasa; the sun's rays too are called Ṛbhus. The Aṅgirases.", 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.17 · The Aṅgirases; the fathers'},
    {'padas': ['virūpāsa idṛṣayasta idgambhīravepasaḥ |', 'te aṅgirasaḥ sūnavaste agneḥ pari jajñire ||', "bahurūpā ṛṣayaḥ | te gambhīrakarmāṇo vā | gambhīraprajñā vā | te'ṅgirasaḥ putrāḥ | te'gneradhijajñire | ityagnijanma |", 'pitaro vyākhyātāḥ | teṣāmeṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 17 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.62.5: various are the seers, of deep power; they are sons of Aṅgiras, born of Agni. The fathers, pitaraḥ.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.18 · The fathers; Atharvans and Bhṛgus'},
    {'padas': ['udīratāmavara utparāsa unmadhyamāḥ pitaraḥ somyāsaḥ |', "asuṃ ya īyuravṛkā ṛtajñāste no'vantu pitaro haveṣu ||", "udīratāmavare | udīratāṃ pare | udīratāṃ madhyamāḥ pitaraḥ | somyāḥ somasaṃpādinaste'suṃ ye prāṇamanvīyuḥ | avṛkā anamitrāḥ | satyajñā vā yajñajñā vā | te na āgacchantu pitaro hvāneṣu |", 'mādhyamiko yama ityāhuḥ | tasmānmādhyamikānpitṝnmanyante |', "aṅgiraso vyākhyātāḥ | pitaro vyākhyātāḥ | bhṛgavo vyākhyātāḥ | atharvāṇo'thanavantaḥ | tharvatiścaratikarmā | tatpratiṣedhaḥ | teṣāmeṣā sādhāraṇā bhavati"], 'num': '|| 18 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.15.1: let the lower, higher and middle soma-loving fathers rise; may they help us at our calls. Yama is of the mid-air, so the fathers are too. Atharvan, "without wavering".', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.19 · Aṅgirases, Navagvas, Atharvans, Bhṛgus; the seers'},
    {'padas': ['aṅgiraso naḥ pitaro navagvā atharvāṇo bhṛgavaḥ somyāsaḥ |', 'teṣāṃ vayaṃ sumatau yajñiyānāmapi bhadre saumanase syāma ||', 'aṅgiraso naḥ pitaraḥ | navagatayo navanītagatayo vā | atharvāṇo bhṛgavaḥ | somyāḥ somasampādinaḥ | teṣāṃ vayam | sumatau kalyāṇyāṃ matau | yajñiyānāmapi caiṣām | bhadre bhandanīye | bhājanavati vā | kalyāṇe manasi | syāmeti |', 'mādhyamiko devagaṇa iti nairuktāḥ | pitara ityākhyānam |', 'athāpyṛṣayaḥ stūyante'], 'num': '|| 19 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.14.6: our fathers the Aṅgirases, Navagvas, Atharvans and Bhṛgus; may we be in their favour. A group of the mid-air, say the etymologists; the fathers, say the story-tellers. The seers too are praised.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.20 · The Vasiṣṭhas; the Āptyas'},
    {'padas': ['sūryasyeva vakṣatho jyotireṣāṃ samudrasyeva mahimā gabhīraḥ |', 'vātasyeva prajavo nānyena stomo vasiṣṭhā anvetave vaḥ ||', 'iti yathā |', 'āptyā āpnoteḥ | teṣāmeṣa nipāto bhavatyaindryāmṛci'], 'num': '|| 20 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 7.33.8: like the sun is their light, like the ocean their depth; none can follow your praise, Vasiṣṭhas. The Āptyas.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.21 · The Āptyas'},
    {'padas': ['stuṣeyyaṃ puruvarpasamṛbhvaminatamamāptyamāptyānām |', 'ā darṣate śavasā sapta dānūnpra sākṣate pratimānāni bhūri ||', 'stotavyam | bahurūpam | urubhūtam | īśvaratamam | āptavyam | āptavyānām | ādṛṇāti | yaḥ | śavasā balena | saptadātṝniti vā | saptadānavāniti vā | prasākṣate | pratimānāni | bahūni | sākṣatirāpnotikarmā'], 'num': '|| 21 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.120.6: I praise the many-formed, the mightiest of the Āptyas, who splits the seven Dānus by his strength.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.22 · The goddesses of the mid-air; Aditi'},
    {'padas': ['athāto madhyasthānāḥ striyaḥ | tāsāmaditiḥ prathamāgāminī bhavati | aditirvyākhyātā | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 22 ||', 'gloss': 'Now the women of the mid-air, first Aditi. Ṛgveda 10.64.5: at the birth of Dakṣa, Aditi, you serve the two kings Mitra and Varuṇa; Aryaman of the unhurried path. Dakṣa is the sun; Aditi daughter of Dakṣa, and Dakṣa son of Aditi.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.23 · How Dakṣa and Aditi beget each other; Agni as Aditi'},
    {'padas': ['dakṣasya vādite janmani vrate rājānā mitrāvaruṇā vivāsasi |', 'atūrtapanthāḥ pururatho aryamā saptahotā viṣurūpeṣu janmasu ||', 'dakṣasya vādite janmani | vrate karmaṇi | rājānau | mitrāvaruṇau | paricarasi | vivāsatiḥ paricaryāyām |', 'haviṣmāṁ āvivāsati |', 'ityāśāstervā | atūrtapanthā atvaramāṇapanthāḥ | bahurathaḥ | aryamādityaḥ | arīnniyacchati | saptahotā | saptāsmai raśmayo rasānabhisannāmayanti | saptainamṛṣayaḥ stuvantīti vā | viṣamarūpeṣu janmasu | karmasūdayeṣu |', 'ādityo dakṣaḥ |', 'ityāhuḥ | ādityamadhye ca stutaḥ | aditirdākṣāyaṇī |', 'aditerdakṣo ajāyata dakṣādvaditiḥ pari |', 'iti ca |', 'tatkathamupapadyate | samānajanmānau syātāmiti | api vā devadharmeṇetaretarajanmānau syātām | itaretaraprakṛtī |', 'agnirapyaditirucyate | tasyaiṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 23 ||', 'gloss': 'They may be born of each other by the nature of gods. Agni too is called Aditi.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.24 · Aditi; Saramā'},
    {'padas': ["yasmai tvaṃ sudraviṇo dadāśo'nāgāstvamadite sarvatātā |", 'yaṃ bhadreṇa śavasā codayāsi prajāvatā rādhasā te syāma ||', 'yasmai tvaṃ sudraviṇo dadāsi | anāgāstvam | anaparādhatvam | adite | sarvāsu karmatatiṣu | āga āṅpūrvādgameḥ | ena eteḥ | kilbiṣaṃ kilbhidam | sukṛtakarmaṇo bhayam | kīrtimasya bhinattīti vā | yaṃ bhadreṇa | śavasā balena | codayasi | prajāvatā ca rādhasā [ dhanena ] te vayamiha syāmeti |', 'saramā saraṇāt | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 24 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.94.15: to whom you give good things, Aditi, sinless in every rite. Āgas, enas, kilbiṣa. Saramā.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.25 · Saramā and the Paṇis'},
    {'padas': ['kimicchantī saramā predamānaḍ dūre hyadhvā jaguriḥ parācaiḥ |', 'kāsmehitiḥ kā paritakmyāsītkathaṃ rasāyā ataraḥ payāṃsi ||', "kimicchantī saramedaṃ prānaṭ | dūre hyadhvā | jagurirjaṅgamyateḥ | parāñcanairañcitaḥ | kā te'smāsvarthahitirāsīt | kiṃ paritakanam | paritakmyā rātriḥ | parita enāṃ takma | takmetyuṣṇanāma | takata iti sataḥ | kathaṃ rasāyā ataraḥ payāṃsīti | rasā nadī rasateḥ śabdakarmaṇaḥ | kathaṃ rasāni tānyudakānīti vā |", 'devaśunīndreṇa prahitā paṇibhirasuraiḥ samūde | ityākhyānam |', 'sarasvatī vyākhyātā | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 25 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.108.1: seeking what has Saramā come here? The way is long. What is your errand, how did you cross the waters of the Rasā? The divine bitch sent by Indra parleyed with the Paṇis. Sarasvatī.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.26 · Sarasvatī'},
    {'padas': ['pāvakā naḥ sarasvatī vājebhirvājinīvatī |', 'yajñaṃ vaṣṭu dhiyāvasuḥ ||', 'pāvakā naḥ sarasvatī | annairannavatī | yajñaṃ vaṣṭu dhiyāvasuḥ karmavasuḥ |', 'tasyā eṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 26 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.3.10: may pure Sarasvatī, rich in rewards, desire our sacrifice.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.27 · Sarasvatī as speech; Vāc'},
    {'padas': ['maho arṇaḥ sarasvatī pra cetayati ketunā |', 'dhiyo viśvā vi rājati ||', 'mahadarṇaḥ sarasvatī pracetayati prajñāpayati ketunā karmaṇā prajñayā vā | imāni ca sarvāṇi prajñānānyabhivirājati | vāgartheṣu vidhīyate | tasmānmādhyamikāṃ vācaṃ manyante |', 'vāgvyākhyātā | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 27 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.3.12: Sarasvatī lights up the great flood and rules all thoughts; so speech of the mid-air. Vāc.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.28 · Speech the queen'},
    {'padas': ['yadvāgvadantyavicetanāni rāṣṭrī devānāṃ niṣasāda mandrā |', 'catasra ūrjaṃ duduhe payāṃsi kva svidasyāḥ paramaṃ jagāma ||', "yadvāgvadanti | avicetanānyavijñātāni | rāṣṭrī devānāṃ niṣasāda [ mandrā ] madanā | catasro'nudiśa ūrjaṃ duduhe payāṃsi | kva svidasyāḥ paramaṃ jagāmeti | yatpṛthivīṃ gacchatīti vā | yadādityaraśmayo harantīti vā |", 'tasyā eṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 28 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 8.100.10: when Speech, queen of the gods, sat down, she milked the four quarters for food; where has her highest gone?', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.29 · All creatures speak her; Anumati and Rākā'},
    {'padas': ['devīṃ vācamajanayanta devāstāṃ viśvarūpāḥ paśavo vadanti |', 'sā no mandreṣamūrjaṃ duhānā dhenurvāgasmānupa suṣṭutaitu ||', 'devīṃ vācamajanayanta devāḥ | tāṃ sarvarūpāḥ paśavo vadanti | vyaktavācaścāvyaktavācaśca | sā no madanānnaṃ ca rasaṃ ca duhānā dhenurvāgasmānupaitu suṣṭutā |', 'anumatī rāketi devapatnyāviti nairuktāḥ | paurṇamāsyāviti yājñikāḥ |', 'yā pūrvā paurṇamāsī sānumatiḥ | yottarā sā rākā |', 'iti vijñāyate |', 'anumatiranumananāt | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 29 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 8.100.11: the gods begot divine Speech; creatures of all forms speak her. Anumati and Rākā: wives of gods, or the two full-moon days. Anumati.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.30 · Anumati; Rākā'},
    {'padas': ['anvidanumate tvaṃ manyāsai śaṃ ca naskṛdhi |', 'kratve dakṣāya no hinu pra ṇa āyūṃṣi tāriṣaḥ ||', "anumanyasvānumate | tvaṃ sukhaṃ ca naḥ kuru | annaṃ ca no'patyāya dhehi | pravardhaya ca na āyuḥ |", 'rākā rāterdānakarmaṇaḥ | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 30 ||', 'gloss': 'Vājasaneyi verse: favour us, Anumati, give happiness, food and long life. Rākā, "the giver".', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.31 · Rākā; Sinīvālī and Kuhū'},
    {'padas': ['rākāmahaṃ suhavāṃ suṣṭutī huve śṛṇotu naḥ subhagā bodhatu tmanā |', 'sīvyatvapaḥ sūcyācchidyamānayā dadātu vīraṃ śatadāyamukthyam ||', 'rākāmahaṃ suhvānāṃ suṣṭutyā hvaye | śṛṇotu naḥ subhagā | bodhatvātmanā | sīvyatvapaḥ prajananakarma | sūcyācchidyamānayā | sūcī sīvyateḥ | dadātu vīram | śatapradam | ukthyaṃ vaktavyapraśaṃsam |', 'sinīvālī kuhūriti devapatnyāviti nairuktāḥ | amāvāsye iti yājñikāḥ |', 'yā pūrvāmāvāsyā sā sinīvālī | yottarā sā kuhūḥ |', 'iti vijñāyate |', 'sinīvālī sinamannaṃ bhavati | sināti bhūtāni | vālaṃ parva vṛṇoteḥ | tasminnannavatī | vālinī vā | vālenevāsyāmaṇutvāccandramāḥ sevitavyo bhavatīti vā |', 'tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 31 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 2.32.4: I call Rākā; may she sew the work with an unbreaking needle and give a hero worth a hundred. Sinīvālī and Kuhū: wives of gods, or the two new-moon days. Sinīvālī.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.32 · Sinīvālī; Kuhū'},
    {'padas': ['sinīvāli pṛthuṣṭuke yā devānāmasi svasā |', 'juṣasva havyamāhutaṃ prajāṃ devi didiḍḍhi naḥ ||', 'sinīvāli | pṛthujaghane | stukaḥ styāyateḥ saṃghātaḥ | pṛthukeśastuke | pṛthuṣṭute vā | yā tvaṃ devānāmasi svasā | svasā su asā | sveṣu sīdatīti vā | juṣasva havyamadanam | prajāṃ ca devi diśa naḥ |', 'kuhūrgūhateḥ | kvābhūditi vā | kva satī hūyata iti vā | kvāhutaṃ havirjuhotīti vā |', 'tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 32 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 2.32.6: broad-hipped Sinīvālī, sister of the gods, give us offspring. Kuhū, "where was she?".', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.33 · Kuhū; Yamī'},
    {'padas': ['kuhūmahaṃ sukṛtaṃ vidmanāpasamasminyajñe suhavāṃ johavīmi |', 'sā no dadātu śravaṇaṃ pitṝṇāṃ tasyai te devi haviṣā vidhema ||', 'kuhūmahaṃ sukṛtaṃ viditakarmāṇamasminyajñe suhvānāmāhvaye | sā no dadātu śravaṇaṃ pitṝṇām | pitryaṃ dhanamiti vā | pitryaṃ yaśa iti vā | tasyai te devi haviṣā vidhemeti vyākhyātam |', 'yamī vyākhyātā | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 33 ||', 'gloss': 'Atharvaveda 7.47.1: I call Kuhū of good deeds; may she give us the fame of the fathers. Yamī.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.34 · Yamī'},
    {'padas': ['anyamū ṣu tvaṃ yamyanya u tvāṃ pari ṣvajāte libujeva vṛkṣam |', 'tasya vā tvaṃ mana icchā sa vā tavādhā kṛṇuṣva saṃvidaṃ subhadrām ||', 'anyameva hi tvaṃ yami | anyastvāṃ pariṣvaṅkṣyate | libujeva vṛkṣam | tasya vā tvaṃ mana iccha | sa vā tava | adhānena kuruṣva saṃvidam | subhadrāṃ kalyāṇabhadrām |', 'yamī yamaṃ cakame | tāṃ pratyācacakṣe | ityākhyānam'], 'num': '|| 34 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.10.14: embrace another, Yamī, as a creeper a tree. Yamī desired Yama, and he refused her; so the story.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.35 · Urvaśī'},
    {'padas': ['urvaśī vyākhyātā | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 35 ||', 'gloss': 'Urvaśī, already explained.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.36 · Urvaśī; the earth'},
    {'padas': ['vidyunna yā patantī davidyodbharantī me apyā kāmyāni |', 'janiṣṭo apo naryaḥ sujātaḥ prorvaśī tirata dīrghamāyuḥ ||', "vidyudiva yā | patantyadyotata | harantī me apyā kāmyāni | udakānyantarikṣalokasya | yadā nūnamayaṃ jāyetādbhyo'dhyapa iti | naryo manuṣyo nṛbhyo hitaḥ | narāpatyamiti vā | sujātaḥ sujātataraḥ | athorvaśī pravardhayate dīrghamāyuḥ |", 'pṛthivī vyākhyātā | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 36 ||', 'gloss': "Ṛgveda 10.95.10: she who flashed like lightning, bringing me the waters' treasures; may Urvaśī lengthen life. Pṛthivī.", 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.37 · The earth; Indrāṇī'},
    {'padas': ['baḷitthā parvatānāṃ khidraṃ bibharṣi pṛthivi |', 'pra yā bhūmiṃ pravatvati mahnā jinoṣi mahini ||', 'satyaṃ tvaṃ parvatānāṃ meghānāṃ khedanaṃ chedanaṃ [ bhedanaṃ ] balamatra dhārayasi pṛthivi | prajinvasi yā bhūmim | pravaṇavati | mahattvena | mahatītyudakavatīti vā |', 'indrāṇī | indrasya patnī | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 37 ||', 'gloss': "Ṛgveda 5.84.1: truly, earth, you bear the breaking of the mountains (clouds). Indrāṇī, Indra's wife.", 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.38 · Indrāṇī'},
    {'padas': ['indrāṇīmāsu nāriṣu subhagāmahamaśravam |', 'nahyasyā aparaṃ cana jarasā marate patiḥ |', 'viśvasmādindra uttaraḥ ||', 'indrāṇīmāsu nāriṣu subhagāmahamaśṛṇavam | na hyasyā aparāmapi samāṃ jarayā mriyate patiḥ | sarvasmād ya indra uttarastametad brūmaḥ |', 'tasyā eṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 38 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.86.11: of these women I have heard Indrāṇī most blessed; her husband shall not die of age.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.39 · Indra and Vṛṣākapi; Gaurī'},
    {'padas': ['nāhamindrāṇi rāraṇa sakhyurvṛṣākaperṛte |', 'yasyedamapyaṃ haviḥ priyaṃ deveṣu gacchati |', 'viśvasmādindra uttaraḥ ||', 'nāhamindrāṇi rame | sakhyurvṛṣākaperṛte | yasyedamapyaṃ haviḥ | apsu śṛtam | adbhiḥ saṃskṛtamiti vā | priyaṃ deveṣu nigacchati | sarvasmād ya indra uttarastametad brūmaḥ |', 'gaurī rocateḥ | jvalatikarmaṇaḥ | ayamapītaro gauro varṇa etasmādeva | praśasyo bhavati |', 'tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 39 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.86.12: I do not delight, Indrāṇī, without my friend Vṛṣākapi. Gaurī, "the shining".', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.40 · Gaurī of a thousand syllables'},
    {'padas': ['gaurīrmimāya salilāni takṣatyekapadī dvipadī sā catuṣpadī |', 'aṣṭāpadī navapadī babhūvuṣī sahasrākṣarā parame vyoman ||', 'gaurīrnirmimāya salilāni | takṣatī kurvatī | ekapadī madhyamena | dvipadī madhyamena cādityena ca | catuṣpadī digbhiḥ | aṣṭāpadī digbhiścāvāntaradigbhiśca | navapadī digbhiścāvāntaradigbhiścādityena ca | sahasrākṣarā bahūdakā | parame vyavane |', 'tasyā eṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 40 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.164.41: the buffalo-cow lowed, shaping the waters, one-footed, two-footed, four-, eight-, nine-footed, of a thousand syllables in the highest heaven: the quarters, the half-quarters, the sun.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.41 · From her the oceans flow'},
    {'padas': ['tasyāḥ samudrā adhi vi kṣaranti tena jīvanti pradiśaścatasraḥ |', 'tataḥ kṣaratyakṣaraṃ tadviśvamupa jīvati ||', 'tasyāḥ samudrā adhivikṣaranti | varṣanti meghāḥ | tena jīvanti digāśrayāṇi bhūtāni | tataḥ kṣaratyakṣaramudakam | tatsarvāṇi bhūtānyupajīvanti |', 'gaurvyākhyātā | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 41 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.164.42: from her the oceans flow and the four quarters live; from her flows the imperishable, by which all lives. Go, the cow.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.42 · The lowing cow'},
    {'padas': ['gauramīmedanu vatsaṃ miṣantaṃ mūrdhānaṃ hiṅṅakṛṇonmātavā u |', 'sṛkvāṇaṃ gharmamabhi vāvaśānā mimāti māyuṃ payate payobhiḥ ||', 'gauranvamīmedvatsam | miṣantamanimiṣantam | ādityamiti vā | mūrdhānamasyābhihiṅṅakaronmananāya | sṛkvāṇaṃ saraṇam | gharmaṃ haraṇam | abhivāvaśānā mimāti māyum | prapyāyate payobhiḥ | māyumivādityamiti vā |', 'vāgeṣā mādhyamikā | gharmadhugiti yājñikāḥ |', 'dhenurdhayatervā | dhinotervā | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 42 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.164.28: the cow lowed after her calf, licking its head; speech of the mid-air, or the cow that yields the gharma milk. Dhenu, the milch cow.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.43 · The milch cow; Aghnyā'},
    {'padas': ['upa hvaye sudughāṃ dhenumetāṃ suhasto godhuguta dohadenām |', "śreṣṭhaṃ savaṃ savitā sāviṣanno'bhīddho gharmastadu ṣu pra vocam ||", 'upahvaye sudohanāṃ dhenumetām | kalyāṇahasto godhugapi ca dogdhyenām | śreṣṭhaṃ savaṃ savitā sunotu na iti | eṣa hi śreṣṭhaḥ sarveṣāṃ savānāṃ yadudakaṃ yadvā payo yajuṣmat | abhīddho gharmaḥ | taṃ su prabravīmi |', 'vāgeṣā mādhyamikā | gharmadhugiti yājñikāḥ |', 'aghnyāhantavyā bhavati | aghaghnīti vā | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 43 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.164.26: I call this easily milked cow; may Savitṛ quicken the best impulse. Aghnyā, "not to be killed".', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.44 · Aghnyā'},
    {'padas': ['sūyavasādbhagavatī hi bhūyā atho vayaṃ bhagavantaḥ syāma |', 'addhi tṛṇamaghnye viśvadānīṃ piba śuddhamudakamācarantī ||', 'sūyavasādinī bhagavatī hi bhava | athedānīṃ vayaṃ bhagavantaḥ syāma | addhi tṛṇamaghnye | sarvadā piba ca śuddhamudakamācarantī |', 'tasyā eṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 44 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.164.40: be fortunate, eating good pasture; eat grass, Aghnyā, and drink pure water at all times.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.45 · The lowing cow; Pathyā Svasti'},
    {'padas': ['hiṅkṛṇvatī vasupatnī vasūnāṃ vatsamicchantī manasābhyāgāt |', 'duhāmaśvibhyāṃ payo aghnyeyaṃ sā vardhatāṃ mahate saubhagāya ||', 'iti sā nigadavyākhyātā |', 'pathyā svastiḥ | panthā antarikṣam | tannivāsāt |', 'tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 45 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.164.27: lowing, mistress of riches, she came seeking her calf. Pathyā Svasti, "wellbeing of the road".', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.46 · Svasti; Uṣas'},
    {'padas': ['svastiriddhi prapathe śreṣṭhā rekṇasvatyabhi yā vāmameti |', 'sā no amā so araṇe ni pātu svāveśā bhavatu devagopā ||', "svastireva hi prapathe śreṣṭhā | rekṇasvatī dhanavatī | abhyeti yā | vasūni vananīyāni | sā no'mā gṛhe | sā niramaṇe | sā nirgamane pātu | svāveśā bhavatu | devī goptrī devāngopāyatviti | devā enāṃ gopāyantviti vā |", 'uṣā vyākhyātā | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 46 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.63.16: Svasti is best on the road; may she guard us at home and abroad. Uṣas, dawn.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.47 · Dawn fled the cart'},
    {'padas': ['apoṣā anasaḥ saratsaṃpiṣṭādaha bibhyuṣī |', 'ni yatsīṃ śiśnathadvṛṣā ||', "apāsaraduṣāḥ | anasaḥ saṃpiṣṭānmeghād bibhyuṣī | ano vāyuraniteḥ | api vopamārthe syāt | anasa iva śakaṭādiva | anaḥ śakaṭam | ānaddhamasmiñcīvaram | anitervā syāt | jīvanakarmaṇaḥ | upajīvantyenat | megho'pyana etasmādeva | yanniraśiśnathat | vṛṣā varṣitā madhyamaḥ |", 'tasyā eṣāparā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 47 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 4.30.10: Dawn fled from the crushed cart, afraid, when the bull struck it. Anas, the cart or the cloud.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': "11.48 · Dawn's broken cart; Iḷā"},
    {'padas': ['etadasyā anaḥ śaye susaṃpiṣṭaṃ vipāśyā |', 'sasāra sīṃ parāvataḥ ||', 'etadasyā ana āśete susaṃpiṣṭam | itaradiva | vipāśi vimuktapāśi | sasāroṣāḥ | parāvataḥ preritavataḥ | parāgatādvā |', 'iḷā vyākhyātā | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 48 ||', 'gloss': "Ṛgveda 4.30.11: Dawn's cart lies crushed by the Vipāś; she fled far. Iḷā.", 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.49 · Iḷā; Rodasī'},
    {'padas': ['abhi na iḷā yūthasya mātā smannadībhirurvaśī vā gṛṇātu |', 'urvaśī vā bṛhaddivā gṛṇānābhyūrṇvānā prabhṛthasyāyoḥ |', 'siṣaktu na ūrjavyasya puṣṭeḥ ||', "abhigṛṇātu na iḷā | yūthasya mātā | [ sarvasya mātā | ] smadabhi nadībhiḥ | urvaśī vā gṛṇātu | urvaśī vā | bṛhaddivā mahaddivā | gṛṇānā | abhyūrṇvānā | prabhṛthasya prabhṛtasya | āyorayanasya [ manuṣyasya ] jyotiṣo vodakasya vā | sevatāṃ no'nnasya puṣṭeḥ |", 'rodasī | rudrasya patnī | tasyā eṣā bhavati'], 'num': '|| 49 ||', 'gloss': "Ṛgveda 5.41.19: may Iḷā, mother of the herd, and Urvaśī with the rivers praise us. Rodasī, Rudra's wife.", 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '11.50 · Rodasī'},
    {'padas': ['rathaṃ nu mārutaṃ vayaṃ śravasyumā huvāmahe |', 'ā yasmintasthau suraṇāni bibhratī sacā marutsu rodasī ||', 'rathaṃ kṣipraṃ mārutaṃ [ meghaṃ ] vayaṃ śravaṇīyamāhvayāmahe | ā yasmintasthau suramaṇīyānyudakāni bibhratī sacā marudbhiḥ saha rodasī'], 'num': '|| 50 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 5.56.8: we call the swift chariot of the Maruts, on which Rodasī stands with the Maruts, bearing delights.', 'prose': True},
